          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मूर्तिः — mūrtiḥ — \"a statue\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मन्दिरे एका प्राचीना मूर्तिः अस्ति। mandire ekā prācīnā mūrtiḥ asti. There is an ancient statue in the temple."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मूर्तिः (mūrtiḥ) comes from the root √mūrch, whose causative MW gives as \"to make settle into a solid form\"; MW sets mūrti, any solid body or material form, an embodiment, an image, among that root's words (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
